prompt_text:
A charming hand-drawn vintage travel scrapbook poster about [北京], designed as a Chinese-language illustrated tourist guide page on warm aged cream paper resting on a wooden tabletop. The composition is a vertical poster with a slightly weathered notebook-page aesthetic, subtle stains, folded corners, washi tape strips, and stamp-like ink smudges in a casual collage layout.

At the top center, prominent bold black Chinese calligraphy reads "[北京]", paired beneath with "[Beijing]" in loose blue brush script, accented by a small red seal stamp and a short geographic description in dark blue handwritten Chinese script on the upper right.

Directly below the title, four taped polaroid-style photos with handwritten English captions are arranged in a casual row: 1. The Forbidden City at sunset glowing in golden light; 2. The Great Wall winding across verdant mountains; 3. Beihai Park lake with willows and the white stupa; 4. A traditional hutong alley with gray brick walls and red lanterns.

